@node D-Bus Methods
@section Method Reference

Reference for every method on @code{org.cmacs.Editor1} as of Phase 1.
D-Bus type signatures: @code{s} string, @code{i} int32, @code{u}
uint32, @code{x} int64, @code{t} uint64, @code{b} bool, @code{d}
double, @code{as} array-of-string, @code{v} variant, @code{o}
object-path, @code{h} file descriptor.

@subsection Eval

Evaluate an arbitrary elisp expression, return its @code{prin1} form.

@example
Eval (s expression) -> (s)
Errors: org.cmacs.Editor1.Error
@end example

@example
gdbus call --session --dest org.cmacs.Editor \
    --object-path /org/cmacs/Editor \
    --method org.cmacs.Editor1.Eval \
    '(format "%s on %s" (emacs-version) (system-name))'
# ('"GNU Emacs 31.0.50 ... on hostname"',)
@end example

This is the universal escape hatch.  Anything reachable from elisp
is reachable from here.

@subsection FindFile

Open a file or URL in the editor.

@example
FindFile (s path) -> ()

gdbus call --session --dest org.cmacs.Editor \
    --object-path /org/cmacs/Editor \
    --method org.cmacs.Editor1.FindFile \
    /etc/hostname
@end example

Equivalent to @code{M-x find-file}, so TRAMP paths work too.

@subsection Message

Display a message in the echo area.

@example
Message (s text) -> ()

gdbus call --session --dest org.cmacs.Editor \
    --object-path /org/cmacs/Editor \
    --method org.cmacs.Editor1.Message \
    "build complete"
@end example

@subsection GiRequire

Load a GObject Introspection namespace into cmacs's GI bridge.

@example
GiRequire (s namespace, s version) -> (b)

gdbus call --session --dest org.cmacs.Editor \
    --object-path /org/cmacs/Editor \
    --method org.cmacs.Editor1.GiRequire \
    GLib 2.0
# (true,)
@end example

@subsection GiCall

Call a function from a previously loaded GI namespace.  Each argument
is passed as a string and read on the cmacs side as a Lisp
expression --- bare words become strings, numbers pass through,
quoted strings stay quoted.

@example
GiCall (s namespace, s function, as args) -> (s)

gdbus call --session --dest org.cmacs.Editor \
    --object-path /org/cmacs/Editor \
    --method org.cmacs.Editor1.GiCall \
    GLib get_user_name '[]'
@end example

@subsection GiListFunctions

@example
GiListFunctions (s namespace) -> (as)

gdbus call --session --dest org.cmacs.Editor \
    --object-path /org/cmacs/Editor \
    --method org.cmacs.Editor1.GiListFunctions \
    GLib | head -3
@end example

@subsection Gowl methods (when --with-cmacs-gowl)

